> It's been 25 years, but no, I don't remember them instakilling at a
> higher rate than they currently do.  A swarming monster that deals
> poison is deadly enough to a weak character.  Basically, I think the
> player characters were weaker in Hack [at least mine were], so deadly
> monsters were extra deadly.  By the time my nethack valkyrie finds a
> swarm of killer bees, the valk has 60+ HP, AC of 0 or better, can
> usually 1-hit kill a bee, usually has a 1-turn way to engrave Elbereth
> (wand of digging?), and oftentimes even already has poison
> resistance.  Maybe it's more similar for a weaker role, but I've only
> played valkyries in nethack.

I don't recall learning how to recover lost strength until much later. 
What I learned was what monsters stung and that I should run from them
and take them out by means other than direct combat.  Even facing them
one by one in a corridor could easily result in getting stung often
enough to gradually lose strength towards zero.

To this day I value MC#3 cloaks over alternatives from this ancient
lesson.


